  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts with the paper bird scene. It passes typecheck, but I couldn't run or render it here, so the flight, flapping and camera behaviour are unverified.\n\n**Bird:** an ellipsoid body and belly, a head with a cone beak and two eyes (white with a dark pupil), and a tail fan of 5 box feathers. Each wing has an inner and an outer segment, joined by a hinge node that can be rotated.\n\n**Flight:**\n- The bird flies a circle of radius 6 at a constant height of 3.6 over an 8-second loop.\n- It banks 0.38 rad toward the centre of the circle and faces its direction of travel.\n- Wings flap twice per second, so a lap is exactly 16 flaps and loops without a jump. The outer segments trail the inner ones by a phase lag so the wing bends, and the body bobs slightly with each flap.\n- Motion is driven by wall-clock time, not accumulated frame time.\n\n**World:**\n- A green ground disc with 17 cone trees (instanced cones and trunks).\n- A sky-coloured background, a neutral environment light and one shadow-casting directional light.\n- The camera orbits outside the circle at radius 13 and height 5.6, trailing the bird by 0.55 rad, and looks at the bird. It is updated each frame with `app.camera.setPose`.\n\n**Camera and loading:**\n- If `app.camera` is unavailable in this build, the camera stays at its starting pose and the bird will leave the view.\n- No external models are loaded.\n- `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()` and two animation frames.\n\n**Unchecked signs:** I derived the bank direction and yaw sign from the engine's right-handed Y-up convention. If the bird banks away from the turn or faces backwards, flip the sign of `BANK` or the yaw.",
